---
import { ink } from "../../lib/ink";
---
<section class="care" aria-labelledby="care-h">
  <h2 id="care-h">What I hold on to</h2>
  <p class="soft">Six knots that haven't slipped yet.</p>
  <ul class="values" role="list">
    <li class="value boil-on-hover">
      <span class="obj boil-target" style="--w:3.4rem"><span class="ink" style={`--src:url(${ink("lens")}); --ar:478/524`}></span></span>
      <h3>Listen first</h3>
      <p>Most bugs begin as misunderstandings. I ask the people, and the designers, before I ask the compiler.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="value boil-on-hover">
      <span class="obj boil-target" style="--w:2.6rem"><span class="ink" style={`--src:url(${ink("broom")}); --ar:433/794`}></span></span>
      <h3>Nothing in the way</h3>
      <p>Speed is not a phase at the end. Every kilobyte is a moment someone spends waiting.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="value boil-on-hover">
      <span class="obj boil-target" style="--w:3rem"><span class="ink" style={`--src:url(${ink("lamp")}); --ar:404/499`}></span></span>
      <h3>Leave a light on</h3>
      <p>Keyboard, screen reader, slow phone, tired eyes. Everyone finds the door.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="value boil-on-hover">
      <span class="obj boil-target" style="--w:2rem"><span class="ink" style={`--src:url(${ink("paperclip")}); --ar:284/419`}></span></span>
      <h3>Hold it together</h3>
      <p>Shared components, clear patterns, one design language, so a whole team can speak without shouting.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="value boil-on-hover">
      <span class="obj boil-target" style="--w:3.6rem"><span class="ink" style={`--src:url(${ink("rubber")}); --ar:535/455`}></span></span>
      <h3>Rub it out</h3>
      <p>Sometimes the best change is a deletion. I'd rather throw away a draft than keep code nobody can read.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="value boil-on-hover">
      <span class="obj boil-target" style="--w:2.9rem"><span class="ink" style={`--src:url(${ink("note")}); --ar:393/465`}></span></span>
      <h3>Leave a note</h3>
      <p>Write down why, not just what, so the next person to open the file isn't left guessing.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>
